 ] ​ ( γ ∈ Γ ) ) ≅ 𝒱 gr ​ ( S ) \mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big)\cong\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(S) obtained above is given by tensoring. Let M M be a graded finitely generated projective R R -module. By § 7.1 , M = M ⁡ ( ϵ ) M=M(\epsilon) for some idempotent matrix ϵ ∈ 𝕄 n × n ⁡ ( R ) \epsilon\in\operatorname{\mathbb{M}}_{n\times n}(R) such that deg ⁡ ( ϵ i ​ j ) = γ j − γ i ​ ( 1 ≤ i , j ≤ n ) \deg(\epsilon_{ij})=\gamma_{j}-\gamma_{i}~(1\leq i,j\leq n) where γ 1 , … , γ n ∈ Γ \gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n}\in\Gamma . Applying the isomorphisms above in reversed order to [ M ] ∈ 𝒱 gr ​ ( R ) / ( [ P ⁡ ( γ ) ] = [ Q ⁡ ( γ ) ] ​ ( γ ∈ Γ ) ) [M]\in\mathcal{V}^{\operatorname{gr}}(R)/\big([P(\gamma)]=[Q(\gamma)]~~(\gamma\in\Gamma)\big) yields (in view of Lemmas 7.2 and 7.3 ) [ M ⁡ ( ϵ ) ] ↦ [ M ⁡ ( ϵ ​ # ​ Γ ) ] ↦ [ M ⁡ ( ϵ ​ # ​ Γ A ) ] ↦ [ M ⁡ ( ϕ A ​ ( ϵ ​ # ​ Γ A ) ) ] ↦ [ M ⁡ ( ψ ⁡ ( ϵ ​ # ​ Γ ) ) ] = [ M ⁡ ( ξ ⁡ ( ϵ ) ​ # ​ Γ ) ] ↦ [ M ⁡ ( ξ ⁡ ( ϵ ) ) ] , [M(\epsilon)]\mapsto[M(\epsilon\#\Gamma)]\mapsto[M(\epsilon\#\Gamma_{A})]\mapsto[M(\phi_{A}(\epsilon\#\Gamma_{A}))]\mapsto[M(\psi(\epsilon\#\Gamma))]=[M(\xi(\epsilon)\#\Gamma)]\mapsto[M(\xi(\epsilon))], where A A is chosen such that all entries of ϵ ​ # ​ Γ \epsilon\#\Gamma lie in R ​ # ​ Γ A R\#\Gamma_{A} , ϵ ​ # ​ Γ A \epsilon\#\Gamma_{A} is just ϵ ​ # ​ Γ \epsilon\#\Gamma viewed as matrix over R ​ # ​ Γ A R\#\Gamma_{A} , and ϕ A : \displaystyle\phi_{A}:{} R # Γ A → R # Γ A ⟨ g ( γ ) , ( g ( γ ) ) − 1 : P A ( γ ) ¯ ≅ Q A ( γ ) ¯ ( γ ∈ A ) ⟩ , \displaystyle{}R\#\Gamma_{A}\to R\#\Gamma_{A}\Big\langle g^{(\gamma)},(g^{(\gamma)})^{-1}:\overline{P_{A}^{(\gamma)}}\cong\overline{Q_{A}^{(\gamma)}}~(\gamma\in A)\Big\rangle, ψ : \displaystyle\psi:{} R ​ # ​ Γ → S ​ # ​ Γ , \displaystyle{}R\#\Gamma\to S\#\Gamma, ξ : \displaystyle\xi:{} R → S \displaystyle{}R\to S are the canonical homomorphisms. It follows from Lemma 7.4 that the isomorphism 𝒱 gr ​ ( R ) / ( [ P ⁡ ( γ 